cff-version: 1.2.0
message: "If you use this dataset, please cite it as below."
type: dataset
title: "atlas: A Synthetic Multi-Party Chat Dataset for Evaluating Memory Systems"
abstract: >-
  atlas is a synthetic dataset for evaluating memory systems that operate in
  multi-party chat. It contains 4,353 messages exchanged by a fictional
  five-person product team across 17 channels over about six weeks, and 415
  questions asked by specific team members at specific points in the
  conversation. Each member can see only the channels they belong to, so the
  correct answer to a question, and what must not be disclosed in it, depend
  on who is asking.
